if(page==="seo")body="<main class=\"page seo-page\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">JOYACELL / "+seo.label+"</p><h1>"+seo.title+"</h1><p class=\"lead\">"+seo.lead+"</p><article id=\"shortlist\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">RESEARCH NOTE</p><h2>Build a shortlist before you make a decision</h2><p>A spreadsheet or category page is most useful when it helps you compare a small number of relevant records. Start with the product type, intended material or design detail; then keep the listing link and the exact variant together. A visual card can help you recognise an item, but it does not replace the live listing.</p><p>Use the same short checklist for each candidate: read the description, record the selected size or colour, compare the available images and note any question that still needs a live answer. This separates early discovery from the later order decision.</p></article><article id=\"qc\"><h2>Keep QC as a later confirmation</h2><p>Warehouse QC belongs after the product and chosen variant have been identified. Treat it as a separate confirmation step: compare what is shown with the listing details you already recorded. Joyacell does not operate the account, payment, warehouse or QC process; those actions are handled in the official platform flow.</p></article><article id=\"parcel\"><h2>Review parcel questions after packing</h2><p>Shipping is not determined by a product image or a spreadsheet row alone. Packed weight, dimensions, route rules and carrier measurement can affect the final parcel. Check the current official information before any transaction, and avoid treating an estimate as a fixed price or delivery time.</p></article><section class=\"seo-checklist\"><h2>A quick research checklist</h2><ul><li>Search by product type, material or style rather than a broad label.</li><li>Keep the live listing and selected variant together.</li><li>Compare listing details with images before using QC as confirmation.</li><li>Review packed-parcel information separately from product discovery.</li></ul><a class=\"button\" href=\""+find("joyagoo research checklist")+"\">"+t[5]+"</a></section></main>";
